            <ArticleTitle>Recent advances in managing gastrointestinal stromal tumor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1689</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12688/f1000research.11118.1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Constitutive activating mutations in KIT and platelet-derived growth factor receptor α ( PDGFRα) are heavily involved in the pathobiology of gastrointestinal stromal tumors (GISTs). This disease has served as an effective &quot;proof-of-concept&quot; model for targeting gain-of-function kinase mutations in cancer. This review discusses the current standard of care in terms of pharmacotherapy in the management of localized and metastatic GISTs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
